# SkillForge web — Vite env vars.
# Only names prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser (import.meta.env).
# Copy this file to web/.env.local (gitignored) and uncomment what you need,
# OR set the same name as a shell env var when running npm run dev.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live backend (real RAG) in dev mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default (unset): dev uses MockChatTransport — recorded UIMessageChunk
# fixtures, zero network. Plain `npm run dev` and the entire vitest suite
# are fully standalone and never require a backend (T-04-04 isolation).
#
# Uncomment to point the dev server at the live Hertz backend (cmd/server
# on :8888) through the vite /api→:8888 proxy. This is the ONLY way to
# end-to-end test real RAG (real embed/retrieve/LLM) while keeping HMR.
# The browser sends UTF-8 JSON via fetch, so this path does NOT hit the
# GBK-curl encoding trap that affected PowerShell-based testing.
#
#   Git Bash:    VITE_REAL_BACKEND=1 npm run dev
#   PowerShell:  $env:VITE_REAL_BACKEND="1"; npm run dev
#   or just uncomment the line below in web/.env.local
# VITE_REAL_BACKEND=1
